WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.969
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Task Starter.

00:00:13.969 --> 00:00:19.937
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:19.937 --> 00:00:23.518
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.518 --> 00:00:27.099
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.099 --> 00:00:35.455
There is a moment that comes before almost every task. The book is closed. The page is blank. And starting feels… big.

00:00:35.455 --> 00:00:45.005
That stuck feeling has company. Everyone feels it — grown-ups too. It is not laziness. It is just how starting feels.

00:00:45.005 --> 00:00:55.749
Here is the secret this tool is built on: you do not have to start the whole thing. You only have to start small.

00:00:55.749 --> 00:01:00.524
A start can shrink until it fits in one tiny move. Let me show you how small a start can be.

00:01:00.524 --> 00:01:11.267
If the task is a book, the start is not reading it. The start is opening it. One cover. That is all.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:22.010
If the task is writing, the start is not the whole story. The start is one word. Any word. It can even be a wobbly one.

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:32.754
If the task is building, the start is not the whole tower. The start is one block, placed on the table.

00:01:32.754 --> 00:01:42.304
One cover. One word. One block. A start so small your hands can do it before the stuck feeling even notices.

00:01:42.304 --> 00:01:43.497
And here is what happens next, most of the time: once the first tiny piece is done, the next piece looks smaller too.

00:01:43.497 --> 00:01:54.241
Starting small is not a small version of the real thing. Starting small IS the real thing. It is how every big thing begins.

00:01:54.241 --> 00:02:04.984
Nobody here is racing. There is no clock on a start, and your start does not have to look like anyone else's.

00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:13.340
If the tiny start still feels too big, shrink it again. Smaller is always allowed. A start can be as small as touching the book.

00:02:13.340 --> 00:02:14.534
You are not behind. You are at the beginning. Beginnings are allowed to be small.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:22.890
Open the book. Write one word. Place one block.

00:02:22.890 --> 00:02:28.859
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:28.859 --> 00:02:33.633
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:39.602
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:39.602 --> 00:02:45.571
You're ready for what's next.
